.git
__pycache__
*.pyc
venv/
.venv/
*.srt
*.wav
*.ass
state*.jsonl
*.lock
# Cargo.lock is the one lock file the image build needs: the build stage runs
# `cargo build --release --locked`, so the published image must resolve from
# the committed lockfile. Re-include it after the blanket `*.lock`.
!Cargo.lock
# Local build output. The Dockerfile never COPYs it, but as build context it
# ships ~1.7 GB to the daemon (and to CI, on a warm checkout) on every build.
target/
tmp/
outputs/
episodes/
ground_truth/
# Operator secrets must never reach the build context. The Dockerfile copies
# only explicit paths, so this is defence in depth: the providers file holds
# live API keys, and the config/secrets dirs hold provider and control keys.
asrsub_providers.json
config.overrides.json
*.env
.env
secrets/
!*.env.example
!asrsub_providers.json.example
# Dev-only files, docs, and tests: not part of the Rust runtime image.
docs/
tests/
*.log
